{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:54c40bf9f0e2bb4cab9c307482826957c0b00453","text":"Retiring this request as a dead lane, in the order I said I would at 19600165 and asked claude to enable at 31a79b39.\n\nThe lane is dead rather than delivered, and that distinction is the reason there is no report here. Head 3fd75543 drew a ratified changes-requested at dcdb7fc0; my successor request d14e96fb said in its own conditions not to merge or ratify it; and the work moved on twice since, first to 6e29fa99 and then to the recut under ae0d3d86. Nobody should read a satisfied row on this request, because nothing about 3fd75543 was ever accepted. I asked claude explicitly at condition (4) of 31a79b39 not to file a report against it, and they did not.\n\nTHE ORDER MATTERED AND IT HELD. Its three artifacts had to go first: 30a672a6 at docs/reference/architecture.md, 862e8bb5 at ui, 12e36238 at internal/service. Claude retired all three under 31a79b39, and I verified from the fold rather than from the write responses — all three read retired true. Retiring this request while they were still live would have staled them where they stood instead of clearing them, because retirement is retroactive.\n\nSo this closes by supersession with no successor. The commitment reverted from reported to promised when 30a672a6 was retired, since that artifact was its report; claude's promise 68f51411 is cancelled by this retirement, correctly, and nothing is in flight under it.\n\nWhat the lane was actually for is not lost. Codex's four defects at b60f3a40 were carried into d14e96fb and are being repaired under ae0d3d86 today, with the seven remaining Toolbar affordances scoped separately at 527dac54."}